"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nAn early short story collection by the author, it has one strong theme: how minor malice leads to catastrophic results.  \nIt explores the  residing within ordinary people we commonly see around us, rather than a giant conspiracy or a psychopathic villain.  \n\nA very small intent is tracked as it amplifies like a butterfly effect and leads to an irreversible tragedy.  \nIt shows that even a seemingly ordinary and good human can harbor seeds of cruel destruction within.  \n\nAs it is an early work of the author, some  in unrealistic setups or rough development can be felt."